Item 04 (Panels in panes) is solved. `python3 ralph_loops/loop0003/gate.py` passes with 1547 tests, and I've marked the item `[x]` and written the iteration 5 entry in PROGRESS.md. Nothing is committed.

**What was built**
- **`python/metacat/qt/hosts.py`:** each graphics window becomes a pane of the main window, showing its Qt canvas. The pane belongs to no window of its own until the main window places it.
  - Windows that don't scroll keep Tk's aspect ratio and are centred in their pane (the Temperature at the top), with the margins in the panel's background colour.
  - The scrolling windows fill the pane beside a scroll bar that is always shown.
  - When a pane changes size, the panel redraws itself through the original's own resize protocol. No panel needs the fallback of just scaling the picture: each panel's resize takes 1–26 ms.
- **`python/metacat/qt/mainwindow.py`:** the splitter layout from item 00, sized for 1080p (the default window is now 1920×1010). The EEG pane is hidden at start, and a 50 ms timer updates every pane.
- **`python/metacat/qt/app.py`:** `python3 -m metacat.qt` now opens with every panel in place. There is no run yet; that is item 05.

**Results**
- Run 7, driven directly with every window in one window, gives exactly its golden trace at the answer. At 300 and 800 codelets the trace matches the golden up to the cap.
- Every pane has items, except the Bottom Themes, which are empty outside justify runs, as in the tkinter snapshots.
- Run 7 with the window resized 14 times during the run still gives its golden trace.
- I looked at the grabs at codelets 300 and 800 and at the answer, pane by pane, next to the tkinter snapshots in `python/tests/snapshots/views/`. They are the same pictures at the panes' sizes, with antialiased text.
- Run 7 to the answer takes 6.8 s with every pane drawn.

**Bugs found and fixed** (each has a test that failed before the fix, and all three are logged in `docs/anomalies_and_quirks.md`)
- **Panels skipped redraws.** The original keeps only one waiting resize for all windows, so most panes would never redraw when they all change size at once. Pane sizes are now passed on one at a time, which makes the startup redraw take about 3 s.
- **Commentary not at its last line.** A pane that grew and shrank back between two updates kept a scroll position Qt had clamped. It now gets a fresh resize in that case.
- **A crash in one resize run out of six.** The engine and the resize thread measure text at the same time on one shared hidden canvas and deleted each other's items. The original and the tkinter GUI have the same race. The Qt hidden canvas now keeps separate items for each thread.

**Open problem for item 05:** with the engine in a separate thread, Qt's drawing stalls for seconds. Each drawn item is a Python call that has to wait for the engine thread to release the GIL. This is why the resize test runs the engine on the GUI thread and resizes every 150 codelets. Mouse clicks on the panes aren't connected yet; that is item 07.

I also updated `docs/divergences.md`, `docs/qt-gui-plan.md` and `python/tests/README.md`.

# result: success in 2812s, 106 turns, cost $7.08
